WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:04.437
- In the last chapter of my
forthcoming happiness book,

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:07.440
I have a quote by Viktor Frankl,

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.908 align:start size:81% position:19%
where he basically
says, you know,

00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:12.245
"Don't pursue directly success.

00:00:12.245 --> 00:00:14.681 align:start size:88% position:13%
It is something that
comes as a consequence."

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:16.315
And I use that because I argue

00:00:16.315 --> 00:00:19.619 align:start size:97% position:3%
that I completely analogize
that to happiness,

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:21.120
and hence, I agree with Jordan.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:24.991 align:start size:84% position:16%
Happiness should be
something that results

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:28.461 align:start size:88% position:13%
from you having adopted
the right mindsets,

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:29.862
the right decisions,

00:00:29.862 --> 00:00:32.332 align:start size:97% position:3%
and so I think you mentioned
purpose and meaning.

00:00:32.332 --> 00:00:33.900
So in one of the chapters

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.602
where I talk about
the two decisions

00:00:35.602 --> 00:00:38.004
that are most likely to impart

00:00:38.004 --> 00:00:39.339
either great amount of misery

00:00:39.339 --> 00:00:41.341
or great amount of
happiness to you,

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:44.577
I say that the choice of
spouse that you choose

00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:47.847 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the choice of
profession that you choose

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:49.682 align:start size:84% position:16%
are the ones that
are going to do that,

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:52.452
either make you more
miserable or happier.

00:00:52.452 --> 00:00:55.355
(intriguing music)

00:00:59.826 --> 00:01:01.428
- I am Dave Rubin,
and joining me today

00:01:01.428 --> 00:01:04.864
is an evolutionary
behavioral scientist,

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:07.200
an author of the brand new book,

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.003
"The Saad Truth
About Happiness,"

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:12.872
and possibly, just possibly.

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:17.476
the most time returning
"Rubin Report" guest,

00:01:17.476 --> 00:01:18.978
my old friend, Gad Saad.

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:20.779 align:start size:84% position:16%
Welcome back to
"The Rubin Report."

00:01:20.779 --> 00:01:22.448
- Oh, Dave, I'm so
happy to be back,

00:01:22.448 --> 00:01:23.950
although I'm a bit dismayed

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:26.519
that it's not sure whether
I'm the most frequent guest.

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:29.488
Please check and get back
to me with those stats.

00:01:29.488 --> 00:01:32.458
- Gad, my team, I have a
very cracked team here.

00:01:32.458 --> 00:01:35.295
They're working overtime
to try to figure this out.

00:01:35.295 --> 00:01:38.865 align:start size:84% position:16%
Right now, we know
