00:02:49.536 --> 00:02:51.905
- But talk to me about how
the tan and the weight loss

00:02:51.905 --> 00:02:53.339
are connected to
this whole thing,

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:55.041
and then we'll get
onto everything else.

00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:57.377
- That's a wonderful way
to start the conversation.

00:02:57.377 --> 00:03:00.280
So the tan comes from
my having just returned

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:03.583
from Portugal with my family,

00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:06.986
and so there's all kinds of
happiness to unpack there.

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:09.822 align:start size:81% position:19%
Number one, having
a great spouse

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:12.491 align:start size:84% position:16%
with whom you can
spend your life with.

00:03:12.491 --> 00:03:13.759
I actually discuss this

00:03:13.759 --> 00:03:15.662
in quite a bit of
detail in the book.

00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:19.499 align:start size:97% position:3%
And you've met her, you
know, on numerous occasions.

00:03:20.432 --> 00:03:22.234
Having great children.

00:03:22.234 --> 00:03:25.671 align:start size:97% position:3%
I know that you recently
became a double twice father,

00:03:25.671 --> 00:03:28.775
so you must now finally
understand what it means

00:03:28.775 --> 00:03:32.945 align:start size:97% position:3%
to have this unconditional,
obsessive love

00:03:32.945 --> 00:03:36.916 align:start size:97% position:3%
for those carrying your genes
into the next generation.

00:03:36.916 --> 00:03:38.618
And regarding the weight,

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:39.852
I actually discuss
that in the book

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:42.822 align:start size:84% position:16%
when I'm discussing
the importance

00:03:42.822 --> 00:03:46.459
of persistence, resilience.

00:03:46.459 --> 00:03:49.728
There's nothing magical about
how I lost about 86 pounds.

00:03:49.728 --> 00:03:53.465
I think, from my heaviest
weight to my lightest,

00:03:53.465 --> 00:03:55.101
I dropped 86 pounds,

00:03:55.101 --> 00:04:00.039
and I did it by repeatedly
making the right decision

00:04:00.039 --> 00:04:01.173
on a daily basis, right?

00:04:01.173 --> 00:04:03.042
So it's little steps.

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:04.477
What is the secret?

00:04:04.477 --> 00:04:09.482 align:start position:0%
Well, number one, I walk between
15 to 20,000 steps a day.

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:11.584
Now, the walking could
be on a stationary bike,

00:04:11.584 --> 00:04:12.952
it could be on an elliptical,

00:04:12.952 --> 00:04:14.687 align:start size:84% position:16%
it could be literally
walking outside.

00:04:14.687 --> 00:04:16.388
But I have my phone with me

00:04:16.388 --> 00:04:19.391 align:start position:0%
so that it's tracking every
single step that I take all day.

00:04:19.391 --> 00:04:23.529
No matter how I feel. I have
to reach 15 to 20,000 steps.

00:04:23.529 --> 00:04:24.797
But of course, as you,

00:04:24.797 --> 00:04:26.766
and probably most of
your listeners know,

00:04:26.766 --> 00:04:29.735 align:start size:88% position:13%
much of your weight loss
or weight maintenance

00:04:29.735 --> 00:04:32.438 align:start size:94% position:6%
comes from what goes into
this gluttonous hole.

00:04:32.438 --> 00:04:33.939
(Dave laughs)

00:04:33.939 --> 00:04:36.008
It's about 90% of
your weight loss

00:04:36.008 --> 00:04:37.610
is going to come
from what you eat,

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:39.912
and so what I try
to do basically

00:04:39.912 --> 00:04:44.984
is hover around 15 to
1,700 calories a day.

00:04:46.318 --> 00:04:49.589
The way that I know that
is because my lovely spouse

00:04:49.589 --> 00:04:52.191 align:start size:81% position:19%
in a very Gestapo,
Nazi-like way,

00:04:52.191 --> 00:04:55.694 align:start size:97% position:3%
keeps track of every single
thing that goes into my mouth.

00:04:55.694 --> 00:04:57.730 align:start size:97% position:3%
And so at the end of the day,
she'll tell me, you know,

00:04:57.730 --> 00:05:01.934
"You're at 1,638 calories,
don't have any more snacks."

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:07.006
And so by having to,

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:10.410
you know, be accountable
to number one, my steps,

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:12.711
number two to my daily calories,

00:05:12.711 --> 00:05:15.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
bit by bit, I woke up
one day, 18 months later,

00:05:15.614 --> 00:05:17.450
as you said, half
the man that I was.

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:18.885
And so there's no secret,

00:05:18.885 --> 00:05:20.920
it's just hard work
and persistence.

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:22.521 align:start size:84% position:16%
- So obviously we'll
dive into a bunch

00:05:22.521 --> 00:05:25.191
of the bullet points of
the book and all that,

00:05:25.191 --> 00:05:28.428 align:start size:97% position:3%
but I have to say, since we've
been doing this since 2018,

00:05:28.428 --> 00:05:30.263
a lot has changed in this world,

00:05:30.263 --> 00:05:32.532 align:start size:88% position:13%
